# Branch process metadata

Copy this file to **`process.md`** on your branch and fill in the values, **or** commit **`process.md.example`** with real `clickup_task` / `branch` values. The workflow reads **`process.md`** first, then **`process.md.example`**.

| Key | Required | Description |
|-----|----------|-------------|
| `branch` | **Yes** (when `clickup_task` is set) | Must match the Git **PR head branch** exactly. The ClickUp comment and automation use this value; the workflow **fails** if it is missing or does not match the PR branch. For OMA work on the feature line, use **`cursor_new_oma_req`**. |
| `clickup_task` | Yes (for ClickUp comments) | Full ClickUp task URL, or the raw task id. |

**Convention for this repo:** set **`branch: cursor_new_oma_req`** when your PR head is **`cursor_new_oma_req`**, so ClickUp always shows the correct branch and commits from the CodeRabbit auto-fix workflow are pushed to that same branch (the PR head).

Example (replace `clickup_task` with your real task):

```text
base_branch: main
branch: cursor_new_oma_req
clickup_task: https://app.clickup.com/t/86d2hrt56
```

Raw task id only is also accepted:

```text
base_branch: main
branch: cursor_new_oma_req
clickup_task: 86d2hrt56
```

Lines must start with the key (optional leading spaces). Use `key: value` on a single line. Inline `#` comments on the same line are stripped.

**Resolution order:** the workflow reads **`process.md`** first, then **`process.md.example`** if the first file is missing or has no `clickup_task`. It does **not** use the PR description, commit links, or repository secrets for the task or branch.

**ClickUp comment:** includes the **task link** and the **`branch`** value from the file that supplied `clickup_task` (not a PR or commit URL). **`git push`** targets the PR head branch, which must be the same as **`branch`** or the job fails.
